          "filename": "Celtic gateway bridge. - Flickr - ohefin.jpg",
          "caption": "This bridge goes over the railway track and road at Holyhead. \nThe Celtic Gateway is a major transport and regeneration project which has resulted in a dramatic new landmark bridge linking the town centre,railway station,and ferry terminal.\nHolyhead is the busiest passenger ferry terminal on the west side of Britain - about 2.3 million people pass through the port each year.The new link makes it far easier for passengers to visit the town.\n\nThe 190 meter steel and concrete footway is supported by 18 steel cables from two large arches 1 meter diameter stainless steel tubing.",
